<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Corner Check</span></h1>
<div class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center">
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3"></div>
<p class="Description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="heading11">Corner Check is when two perpendicular planes (including the corner between them) of the alignment block are scanned.</span> <span class="heading11" lang="EN-US">For example plane 1 and plane 5. To each plane of the scan data is fitted one plane and an error map is computed.</span> The results can be checked against specification. This specification will vary with localiser performance and sensor type.</p>
<p class="stepstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Procedure</span></p>
<table class="TableGrid" style="border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<col>
<col>
<col>
<tr>
<td class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;"><img src="../images/image001.gif" width="168px" height="223px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></font></span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/Check_Corner1.gif" width="168px" height="280px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">Scan plane 1 horizontally in one continuous motion, keeping the sensor approximately normal to the surface.</font></span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">Pause the scan.</font></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;"><img src="../images/image002.gif" width="171px" height="254px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></font></span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/Check_Corner2.gif" width="169px" height="290px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">Scan plane</font></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">5</font></span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">horizontally in one continuous motion, keeping the sensor approximately normal to the surface.</font></span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">Pause the scan.</font></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/image003.gif" width="232px" height="236px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/Check_Corner3.gif" width="336px" height="220px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">Scan the corner between plane 1 and plane 5 in the same direction as above, keeping the sensor at 45 degrees to the surface.</font></span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;"><font size="1" style="font-size:9pt;">Make sure the 1<sup>st</sup> and the 3<sup>rd</sup> scans as well as the 2<sup>nd</sup> and the 3<sup>rd</sup> scans have overlapping areas.</font></span></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="whs4">
<p class="caption">FARO / CimCore</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs4">
<p class="caption">K-Scan</p>
</td>
<td class="whs4">
<p class="caption">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Above</b></span>: The different scanning stages of the certification and the relevant ModelMaker positions and scanning movements. <span lang="EN-US">&#160;</span></p>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">For plane 1:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Use the lasso to select and delete any points scanned in that do not lie on surface of the plane.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Use the lasso <span lang="EN-US">again to select the plane 1 scan as close to the corner as possible.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Select the <span class="Path">Measure &gt; Geometry &gt; Plane</span> menu item.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Press '<b style="font-weight:normal;">OK'</b>. The statistics dialogue will now appear:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Normal"><span lang="EN-US">&#160;</span><img src="fit_plane.jpg" width="215px" height="350px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></p>
<ul type="disc" class="whs12">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Check that the limits match the values specified for the system.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">RMS limits for FARO Gold arm</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP166724865" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="whs13"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Probe RMS</b></span>: depends on the arm accuracy. For FARO Gold arm is recommended the max RMS value to be less than 0.015mm.</p>
<p class="whs13"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Stripe RMS</b></span>: this value depends on the used sensor. Here follows a table with recommended max values for different sensors (in case a FARO Gold arm is used in the system):</p>
<p class="whs13">&#160;</p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="487" class="whs14">
<col>
<col>
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs15">
<td class="whs16">
<p class="normal-table-func">Sensor</p>
</td>
<td class="whs17">
<p class="normal-table">X35 / Z35</p>
</td>
<td class="whs17">
<p class="normal-table">X70 / Z70</p>
</td>
<td class="whs18">
<p class="normal-table">X140 / Z140</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs15">
<td class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func">Stripe</p>
</td>
<td class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table">0.020</p>
</td>
<td class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table">0.025</p>
</td>
<td class="whs21">
<p class="normal-table">0.030</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<ul type="disc" class="whs12">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Repeat the same procedure for plane 5.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>

